  "notes": "Digitized from the Kodak E-4070 datasheet of December 2017, the paper every one of the six film sheets names. Status A curves for a 0.5 s sensitometric exposure; the sheet does not say what light the sensitometer used, so the enlarger here is a stand-in and lab balance acts on a relative scale. Past D-max the curves fall by up to 0.020 D (red, from log H -0.40 to -0.15); that is printed on the sheet and kept, so a loader that wants a monotonic curve has to clip it. The dye curves are the sheet's own unit-peak curves and read 0.998, 1.000 and 1.000 on the 5 nm grid. No granularity and no MTF on the sheet.",
  "source": {
    "publication": "E-4070",
